 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 27 \u2014 Prompt Portability and Multi-Model Systems\n",
    "\n",
    "## Scenario\n",
    "Your company has hardcoded hundreds of API calls to a single AI provider throughout your codebase. \n",
    "\n",
    "**The Problem:** The provider suffers a massive outage. Your entire application goes down because you are vendor-locked. Furthermore, migrating to a new model requires rewriting business logic.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The Solution:** We must decouple the application from the model. We do this by defining a strict **Contract** (a Pydantic schema) and using **Model Adapters** to translate the contract into provider-specific prompts. We then use a **Router** to implement automatic fallbacks."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from typing import List, Optional\n",
    "from pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n",
    "from google import genai\n",
    "from google.genai import types\n",
    "\n",
    "client = genai.Client()\n",
    "PRIMARY_MODEL = 'gemini-2.5-flash'\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: The Universal Contract\n",
    "\n",
    "This Pydantic schema is the ONLY thing the core application knows about. It knows nothing about \"system instructions\" or \"XML tags.\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class FinancialSummary(BaseModel):\n",
    "    company_name: str\n",
    "    revenue_trend: str = Field(description=\"UP, DOWN, or FLAT\")\n",
    "    key_risks: List[str] = Field(description=\"List of risk factors mentioned\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: The Model Adapters\n",
    "\n",
    "Adapters take the raw input, apply model-specific prompting techniques, call the API, and return the Pydantic contract."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class GeminiAdapter:\n",
    "    def generate_summary(self, text: str, force_failure: bool = False) -> FinancialSummary:\n",
    "        if force_failure:\n",
    "            raise Exception(\"503 Service Unavailable: Primary provider is down!\")\n",
    "            \n",
    "        print(\"[GeminiAdapter] Calling Gemini API...\")\n",
    "        # Gemini excels with clear Markdown block instructions\n",
    "        prompt = f\"Extract financial data from the text.\\n\\nText:\\n{text}\"\n",
    "        \n",
    "        response = client.models.generate_content(\n",
    "            model=PRIMARY_MODEL,\n",
    "            contents=prompt,\n",
    "            config=types.GenerateContentConfig(\n",
    "                temperature=0.0,\n",
    "                response_mime_type=\"application/json\",\n",
    "                response_schema=FinancialSummary,\n",
    "            )\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        return FinancialSummary.model_validate_json(response.text)\n",
    "\n",
    "class FallbackAdapter:\n",
    "    def generate_summary(self, text: str) -> FinancialSummary:\n",
    "        print(\"[FallbackAdapter] Calling secondary provider (Simulated)...\")\n",
    "        # A different provider might require XML tags instead of Markdown\n",
    "        prompt = f\"<instruction>Extract financial data</instruction>\\n<text>{text}</text>\"\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Simulating a successful response from a secondary provider\n",
    "        return FinancialSummary(\n",
    "            company_name=\"Acme Corp (From Fallback)\", \n",
    "            revenue_trend=\"DOWN\",\n",
    "            key_risks=[\"Supply chain issues\"]\n",
    "        )\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: The Multi-Model Router\n",
    "\n",
    "The Router ties it together, trying the primary and falling back to the secondary on failure."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class ModelRouter:\n",
    "    def __init__(self):\n",
    "        self.primary = GeminiAdapter()\n",
    "        self.fallback = FallbackAdapter()\n",
    "        \n",
    "    def get_summary(self, text: str, simulate_outage: bool = False) -> FinancialSummary:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            return self.primary.generate_summary(text, force_failure=simulate_outage)\n",
    "        except Exception as e:\n",
    "            print(f\"\\n\ud83d\udea8 [ROUTER ALERT] Primary model failed: {e}\")\n",
    "            print(\"\ud83d\udd04 [ROUTER] Failing over to secondary model...\\n\")\n",
    "            return self.fallback.generate_summary(text)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: Testing the Portability\n",
    "\n",
    "We run the router normally, and then we simulate a massive cloud outage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "router = ModelRouter()\n",
    "document = \"Acme Corp saw a 20% drop in revenue this quarter due to supply chain disruptions in Asia.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== TEST 1: Normal Operations ===\")\n",
    "result_1 = router.get_summary(document)\n",
    "print(result_1)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== TEST 2: Primary Provider Outage ===\")\n",
    "result_2 = router.get_summary(document, simulate_outage=True)\n",
    "print(result_2)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "Because the application logic only expects a `FinancialSummary` object, it **doesn't care** which model actually fulfilled the request.\n",
    "\n",
    "By using **Pydantic Contracts** and **Model Adapters**, we achieved true Prompt Portability, allowing us to survive a vendor outage with zero application downtime."
   ]
  }
 ],
